*.log

# AZ training artifacts (checkpoints, replay buffer) — az_model.npz ships separately
games/spender/ai/offline/checkpoints/
games/spender/ai/offline/checkpoints*/

# AZ offline-tooling scratch outputs (regenerated by the h3_*/s_measure/turns_ab harnesses)
games/spender/ai/offline/*.out
# turns_table_s.json is written by valuation3 (serving) next to itself via dirname(__file__)
games/spender/ai/serving/turns_table_s.json

# one-off AI experiment run scripts (self-labeled throwaway; not part of the serving path)
games/spender/ai/ablation_run.py
games/spender/ai/sweep_run.py
games/spender/ai/confirm_c2.py

# net-retrain investigation scratch (harvested caches + fitted leaf model; regenerable)
games/spender/ai/offline/*cache*.npz
# leaf_model.npz is loaded by vsearch (serving) from its own dir via dirname(__file__)
games/spender/ai/serving/leaf_model.npz

# SQLite databases (contain user data)
*.db
# ...and the sidecars sqlite writes beside them. `*.db` alone let a
# `users.db-journal` through, which `npm run screens` leaves behind every time
# it boots a backend -- so a `git add -A` after running the gates would have
# committed one.
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Cython build artifacts — the hot-path module (valuation3) is compiled in the Docker build, never committed
games/spender/ai/serving/valuation3.c
games/spender/ai/serving/*.so
games/spender/ai/serving/*.pyd
# MSVC byproducts of a local in-place `cythonize -i` build (dev box now has a compiler)
games/spender/ai/serving/*.obj
games/spender/ai/serving/*.exp
games/spender/ai/serving/*.lib

# Cython/setuptools build temp dir
build/

# Stray local AI-harness run logs at the repo root (config_selfgate / background runs
# redirected to engine_stk_*.out/.err) — scratch, regenerated per run
/engine_stk_*.out
/engine_stk_*.err

# duel-core: build output + generated parity fixtures + arena run logs
rust-cores/duel-core/target/
# Scratch build dirs: cargo cannot relink an .exe another process is running, so a
# long gate/harvest run blocks rebuilds. Building to a side dir keeps both alive.
rust-cores/duel-core/target-*/
rust-cores/duel-core/fixtures/
rust-cores/duel-core/*.out

# Playwright/screens debug output (screenshots are ORBIT_SHOTS-gated local artifacts)
webapp/test-results/

# Local Orbit neural campaign data, checkpoints, tools and benchmark artifacts.
# These now live UNDER THE GAME, like every other game's AI artifacts
# (`games/spender/ai/offline/...`). They used to be ~40 `.orbit-*` directories in
# the repo root holding 5.8 GB, of which 3.1 GB was dead cargo build output from
# one-off `--target-dir` experiments.
# ...but the RUN SCRIPTS themselves are tracked, and the outputs are not. The
# scripts are the experimental protocol -- what was compared, at what budget,
# with which controls and non-vacuity checks -- and on 2026-09-14 all 19 of them
# existed in no commit at all. A campaign whose method lives only on one disk
# cannot be audited, reproduced, or recovered.
#
# THE DIRECTORY FORM CANNOT EXPRESS THIS. `games/orbit/ai/runs/` excludes the
# directory, and git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a later
# `!.../*.sh` would never be consulted. Excluding the CONTENTS instead leaves the
# directory itself readable, and the negation then works. The `*` still matches
# every result subdirectory, so the 5.8 GB of checkpoints and arena reports this
# rule was written for stays out.
#
# They only became worth tracking once they stopped hardcoding one machine's
# path: `REPO` now derives from ${BASH_SOURCE[0]}, so a script runs in whichever
# worktree it sits in.
games/orbit/ai/runs/*
!games/orbit/ai/runs/*.sh
# The old root location, kept so a stale checkout or an older tool cannot start
# re-littering the root. NOTE the missing trailing slash on the second pattern:
# `.orbit-*/` matched DIRECTORIES only, so the root `.orbit-*.json` arena reports
# were left untracked and visible in `git status` forever.
.orbit-*
# pytest --basetemp scratch. Was `.pytest-orbit-*/` only, which missed the
# `.pytest-tmp*`, `.pytest-final-run` and `.pytest-*-run` dirs the same commands
# create; they end up unreadable on Windows and then noise up `git status` with
# "could not open directory" warnings on every invocation.
.pytest-*

# BGG Filter harvest scratch (regenerable; only the trimmed payload is committed)
bggfilter/tools/cache/
bggfilter/tools/results_all.json
